{"step_index":293,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-11T02:44:57Z","input_tokens":4138,"cache_read_tokens":243887,"output_tokens":686,"content":"### 1. How Many Languages Does It Support?\nCurrently, it supports **only Python (1 language)**.\n\nWhy? Because the execution engine ([`app_build/engine.js`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/engine.js) & [`app_build/engine.py`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/engine.py)) is specifically engineered around **Python's AST, indentation rules, OOP (`self`, `__init__`), and object-reference memory model (`Name → @Address → Value`)**—similar to how the Thonny IDE works for Python.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Ready-to-Post LinkedIn Note (Copy & Paste)\n\n> 🚀 **Built a Zero-API Python & DSA Code Flow Visualizer (\"Teach Me This Code\")!**\n>\n> Most beginners struggle with DSA not because of syntax, but because they can’t *see* how variables, loops, recursion, and memory actually change step-by-step.\n>\n> So I built an interactive, **100% offline Python Execution & Memory Visualizer**—with **zero external AI APIs or paid keys**—inspired by the educational mechanics of the Thonny IDE.\n>\n> ✨ **Key Engineering Highlights:**\n> 🔹 **Step-by-Step Sub-Expression Evaluator:** Breaks down complex lines into internal sub-steps (including short-circuit `and`/`or` evaluation) so you see *how* Python calculates every value before assigning it.\n> 🔹 **Visual Stack & Heap Memory Model (`Name → @Addr → Value`):** Isolates **Global vs. Local Scopes** on the Call Stack and maps variable references to Heap memory addresses with live Reference Counting & Visual Garbage Collection.\n> 🔹 **Complete DSA Iteration & Dry-Run Explorer:** Automatically groups execution by loop iterations, OOP method calls (`Stack`, `LinkedList`), or recursive frames, alongside a full clickable **Step 1 → N Dry-Run Table**.\n> 🔹 **100% Deterministic & Offline:** Runs entirely on a custom AST + execution tracer and rule-based explanation engine.\n>\n> Built to make learning Python and cracking Data Structures & Algorithms intuitive for everyone! 💻🔥\n>\n> `#Python` `#DSA` `#SoftwareEngineering` `#CodingEducation` `#WebDevelopment` `#ComputerScience` `#BuildInPublic`","thinking":"This system is currently designed to operate specifically within the Python programming language due to its specialized execution engine and memory management model. The core components, including the abstract syntax tree (AST) evaluator and the stack/heap memory model, are built to function with Python's execution characteristics. This focused design means it is inherently language-specific.\n\n\n"}
